    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί-χρονος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, in
		Metre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of two quantities,
				common,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.737e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.100
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ διχρόνων,</span> title of
			treatise by Hdn.Gr. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>consisting of two short syllables,</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				3.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
				139.20
			</span></i>: metaph. of the pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Syn. Puls.</u>
				4.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>equivalent to two time-units,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				<u>Proll.Heph.</u>
				p.87C.
			</span></i>
		</div>
